cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper (see references below)."

title: "EQUISITE: equity-aware vertiport siting for urban air mobility"

abstract: >-
  EQUISITE (EQUIty-aware SITE selection) is a four-stage framework for siting urban air
  mobility vertiports, applied to Chengdu, China. Stage 1 screens candidate sites from
  OpenStreetMap, satellite-derived building heights and terrain, separately for rooftops
  and for ground parcels, which have opposite cost structures. Stage 2 stratifies demand:
  population is redistributed onto buildings, clustered by an income proxy, and converted
  to trips by a mode-choice model. Stage 3 solves policy-constrained cases exactly, as
  0-1 integer programs. Stage 4 searches the unconstrained trade-off surface with a
  from-scratch NSGA-II over four objectives: unserved demand, total access time,
  worst-group access time, and capital cost. The equity objective, the mean access time
  of the worst-off income group, is optimised directly rather than checked after the
  fact, and rooftop and ground vertiports are modelled as distinct facility classes
  within one optimisation.

type: software

